@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+# Cloud9 FR-Spec + portable MoE expert pool (2026-10-27)
+
+This is an isolated laboratory branch of the Atomic 2.0 engine, **not production**.
+
+Source for the portable expert pool: `memoriaru/llama.cpp`, branch `moe-expert-pool`, commit `555d1ec9daa4564cb06adb39c469acfdcd1d1e93`; introductory commit `f7dd595` and subsequent corrective commits through `555d1ec`. Credit to original authors and maintainers; preserve their licenses and acknowledgements. Upstream: https://github.com/memoriaru/llama.cpp/tree/moe-expert-pool . RFC: https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/discussions/28248 .
+
+Ported pool API/scheduler, expert-id table remapping, persistent GPU slots, budget rails, tests and CLI into Atomic 2.0 laboratory base `0780e182` (which already has native Qwen4Exp FR-Spec 65K d2t, split projections, mmap-lazy PLE and CPU experts). The native adaptive `--moe-cache` is separate from experimental `--moe-expert-cache`; compare by setting `--moe-cache off` before testing the new pool.
+
+Current evidence: Vulkan `test-expert-pool` PASSES on AMD Radeon780M RADV, and synthetic Qwen4Exp `test-llama-archs -a qwen4exp` PASSES. A full target+draft real inference with the new pool is **NOT YET QUALIFIED**: Cloud9 embedding slots remain active, and its benchmark guardian correctly refuses contested runs. No score or production deployment is claimed. The previous full AD4.27+FR-Spec Atomic2 baseline remains 2.685 t/s best warm three-task complete.
